--- a/docs/reference.md
+++ b/docs/reference.md
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ An append-only log of keyed events, stored as a directory of segment files.
 
 | Field | Value | Meaning |
 |---|---|---|
-| `segment.name` | `{base_offset:020d}.log` | One file per segment, named by the offset of its first record. |
+| `segment.name` | `{base_offset:020d}.seg` | One file per segment, named by the offset of its first record. Segments named `{base_offset:020d}.log` (before 0.4) are refused. |
 | `segment.magic` | `EVLG` | First four bytes of every segment. |
 | `segment.version` | `2` | Format version byte after the magic. Other versions, including 1, are refused. |
 | `segment.header` | `magic(4) version(u8) base_offset(u64)` | Fixed header before the first record. |
@@ -88,6 +88,7 @@ Every error derives from `EventLogError`. Messages:
 | `ValueTooLarge` | `value of {size} bytes exceeds max_value_bytes {limit}` | Value longer than `max_value_bytes`. |
 | `RecordTooLarge` | `record of {size} bytes exceeds segment_bytes {limit}` | An encoded record that would not fit even in an empty segment; nothing is written. |
 | `OffsetOutOfRange` | `offset {offset} is outside {first}..{next}` | Replaying from before the first offset or past the next one. |
+| `LegacySegmentName` | `{segment}: segment files now use the .seg suffix` | Opening a directory holding a segment named with the old `.log` suffix; names the lowest-offset one. |
 | `UnsupportedFormat` | `{segment}: unsupported format version {version}` | Opening a segment with another format version. |
 | `NotASegment` | `{segment}: not an event log segment` | Bad magic or a file shorter than the header. |
 | `CorruptRecord` | `corrupt record at position {position} in {segment}` | Checksum or framing failure. |
